@startuml scaling-resilience-topology
top to bottom direction
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowColor #334155
skinparam ArrowFontColor #1E293B
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam PackageBorderColor #64748B
skinparam PackageFontColor #0F172A
skinparam PackageFontStyle bold
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #334155
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #334155
skinparam QueueBorderColor #334155
skinparam nodesep 45
skinparam ranksep 55
skinparam padding 8

title **Ariel System — Elastic Horizontal Scaling, Resilience4j & High-Availability Topology**\n//How the System Absorbs 100x Traffic Spikes & Survives Infrastructure Failures with Zero Data Loss//\n

' ==============================================================================
' LAYER 1: TRAFFIC SHIELD & MULTI-AZ ACTIVE-ACTIVE DISTRIBUTION
' ==============================================================================
package "1. Edge Traffic Shield & Multi-AZ Pod Topology — Why: Survive Full Zone Outages & Shed Overload Early" as Tier1 #F1F5F9 {
    component "**Global Multi-AZ Ingress & Load Balancer**\n//Role: Active-Active Cross-Zone Traffic Distribution (AZ-A / AZ-B / AZ-C)//\n• **Zero Single Point of Failure**: Pods spread evenly via K8s ""topologySpreadConstraints"" & ""podAntiAffinity""\n• **Graceful Rolling Updates**: Readiness/Liveness/Startup probes + 30s connection draining (""server.shutdown=graceful"")" as IngressLB #CBD5E1
    component "**Edge Rate Limiter & Idempotency Barrier**\n//Role: Backpressure & Duplicate Suppression at the Perimeter//\n• **Token-Bucket Rate Limiting**: Atomic Redis Lua script throttles abusive tenants (""HTTP 429 ProblemDetail"")\n• **Idempotency Lock**: Atomic ""SET NX EX"" prevents duplicate transactions during client retry storms" as EdgeShield #93C5FD
    IngressLB -right-> EdgeShield : Filtered & Balanced\nMulti-AZ Traffic
}

' ==============================================================================
' LAYER 2: DUAL ELASTIC HORIZONTAL AUTOSCALING LOOPS (HPA vs KEDA)
' ==============================================================================
package "2. Elastic Horizontal Compute Scaling — Why: Scale Write/Read APIs & Event Consumers Independently" as Tier2 #EFF6FF {
    component "**Kubernetes HPA (Metric-Driven Autoscaler)**\n//Target: Stateless API Pods//\n• **Triggers**: CPU > 70%, Memory,\n  Prometheus RPS & P99 Latency > 12ms\n• **Scale Range**: **3 -> 100+ Pods** across 3 AZs" as HPA #FCD34D

    component "**Synchronous Fast-Path & CQRS API Fleet**\n//Services: Gateway, Ingestion, Risk Engine, Ledger, Query//\n• **Java 25 Virtual Threads**: Millions of concurrent I/O calls without thread-pool starvation\n• **Generational ZGC**: ""< 0.5ms"" GC pauses under heavy allocation\n• **Spring AOT + AppCDS**: ""< 2s"" cold pod startup during scale-out bursts" as ApiFleet #BFDBFE

    component "**Asynchronous Stream Worker Fleet**\n//Service: Ariel Stream Processor Pods//\n• **Java 25 Stream Gatherers**: ""windowFixed(100)"" micro-batching\n• **Parallel Sink Fan-Out**: ""StructuredTaskScope"" writes to\n  ScyllaDB, ClickHouse & Iceberg concurrently" as StreamFleet #BFDBFE

    component "**KEDA (Event-Driven Autoscaler)**\n//Target: Kafka Consumer Group Pods//\n• **Trigger**: Apache Kafka Consumer Lag\n  ""> 5,000 msgs/partition"" on validated topics\n• **Scale Range**: **3 -> 64 Pods** (matches partitions)" as KEDA #FCD34D

    HPA -right-> ApiFleet : Scales Out/In\non RPS & Latency
    KEDA -left-> StreamFleet : Scales Out/In\non Kafka Lag
}

' ==============================================================================
' LAYER 3: RESILIENCE4J IN-POD FAULT ISOLATION PIPELINE
' ==============================================================================
package "3. Resilience4j Fault-Tolerance Pipeline — Why: Prevent Cascading Failures & Downstream Overload" as Tier3 #FEF3C7 {
    component "**1. Semaphore Bulkhead & TimeLimiter**\n//Role: Concurrency Isolation & Fast Timeout//\n• **SemaphoreBulkhead**: Caps max concurrent Virtual Threads\n  calling each dependency (prevents DB/HTTP pool exhaustion)\n• **TimeLimiter**: Strict ""5ms"" budget on Risk checks;\n  cancels slow sub-tasks immediately via ""StructuredTaskScope""" as Bulkhead #FDE68A

    component "**2. Sliding-Window Circuit Breaker**\n//Role: Fail-Fast & Automatic Recovery//\n• Trips **OPEN** when error rate ""> 50%"" or slow-call rate ""> 80%""\n• **Graceful Fallback**: Serves stale L1 Caffeine rules or\n  routes non-critical telemetry to async buffer when tripped" as CircuitBreaker #FCD34D

    component "**3. Exponential Backoff Retry + Jitter**\n//Role: Thundering-Herd Prevention//\n• Retries only transient network/timeout errors on idempotent calls\n• Adds randomized jitter (""±50%"") so scaled pods never retry in sync" as RetryJitter #FDE68A

    Bulkhead -right-> CircuitBreaker : Passes Bounded\nFast Calls
    CircuitBreaker -right-> RetryJitter : Wraps Transient\nFailures
}

' ==============================================================================
' LAYER 4: STATEFUL HIGH-AVAILABILITY, REPLICATION & DLQ DURABILITY
' ==============================================================================
package "4. Stateful Data HA, Quorum Replication & Zero-Data-Loss Durability — Why: RPO = 0 & Self-Healing Storage" as Tier4 #ECFDF5 {
    database "**L1 Caffeine + L2 Redis 8 Cluster**\n//Multi-AZ Cache & Coordination HA//\n• **Topology**: 3 Master Shards + 3 Replicas\n  spread across AZ-A, AZ-B, AZ-C\n• **Failover**: Automatic cluster promotion (<2s)\n• **Coherence**: Redis Pub/Sub broadcasts\n  evictions to all pod L1 caches" as RedisHA #A7F3D0

    database "**PostgreSQL 17 HA (Patroni / Citus)**\n//ACID Ledger & Transactional Outbox HA//\n• **Primary (AZ-A) <-> Sync Standby (AZ-B)**:\n  Synchronous commit guarantees **Zero Data Loss (RPO=0)**\n• **Async Replicas (AZ-C)**: Read offload\n• **HikariCP Bounded Pool**: Protects DB connections\n  from 100+ scaled Virtual Thread pods" as PostgresHA #6EE7B7

    database "**ScyllaDB & ClickHouse Clusters**\n//Distributed Big Data & OLAP HA//\n• **ScyllaDB**: Masterless ring across 3 AZs\n  (""Replication Factor = 3"", ""LOCAL_QUORUM"")\n• **ClickHouse**: ""ReplicatedMergeTree"" shards\n  with automatic background compaction" as OlapHA #34D399

    queue "**Apache Kafka (KRaft) + DLQ Pipeline**\n//Durable Event Backbone HA//\n• **Quorum**: 3+ Brokers across AZs, ""RF = 3"",\n  ""min.insync.replicas = 2"", Producer ""acks = all""\n• **Self-Healing Consumers**: Non-blocking retry\n  topics (""1s -> 5s -> 30s"" backoff) -> isolates\n  poison pills into **""ariel.dlq""** with trace headers" as KafkaHA #F9A8D4

    RedisHA -[hidden]right-> PostgresHA
    PostgresHA -[hidden]right-> OlapHA
    OlapHA -[hidden]right-> KafkaHA
}

' ==============================================================================
' CLEAN LAYER-TO-LAYER CONNECTIONS (TOP -> BOTTOM, ZERO CROSSINGS)
' ==============================================================================

EdgeShield -down-> ApiFleet : Verified Requests\nDispatched to Pods

ApiFleet -down-> Bulkhead : Outbound Service & DB Calls\nEnter Resilience Pipeline
StreamFleet -down-> RetryJitter : Sink & Broker Calls Protected\nby Backoff & CircuitBreaker

Bulkhead -down-> RedisHA : Sub-1ms Cache &\nVelocity Lookups
CircuitBreaker -down-> PostgresHA : ACID Ledger Commit +\nOutbox Event Write
RetryJitter -down-> OlapHA : Parallel Micro-Batch\nAnalytical Writes
RetryJitter -down-> KafkaHA : Outbox Relay & DLQ\nEvent Publishing
KafkaHA -up-> KEDA : Reports Partition\nConsumer Lag

@enduml
